          "title": "You'll want to know: zúqiú",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zúqiú — \"football; soccer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ xǐhuan zúqiú — I love football."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zúqiú is built from zú 'foot' and qiú 'ball', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsjowk and gjuw (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). The dictionary glosses gjuw as 'fine jade', and under another way of writing it as a ball of fur that is struck."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for what I like."
